  concept: 'Authored objective: Build the 16-layer network.

    Authored requirement:
    Connect 208 native route pairs, 68 legal training spans and the separate W209
    jumper.

    General teaching principle: PCB acceptance depends on the authored
    footprints, nets, layers, clearances and route constraints; visual appearance
    alone is insufficient.

    Only fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish
    that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A multilayer road map helps visualize routing, but electrical continuity
    and constraints still require checks.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: A visually connected trace is not proof of correct net connectivity
    or clearance.
